{
  "requirement": "When a model tool explicitly reads an excluded file, the harness MUST return a tool error naming the path and the reason\nit cannot be read, add no evidence input, and continue the assessment.\nDiscovery and search MUST omit excluded files. Malformed tool\narguments and ordinary read failures MUST also return explanatory tool errors.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover each obligation in `requirements.authoring.read_denial`.\n\n**1. Explicit read of an excluded file returns a tool error naming the path and reason, adds no evidence input, and the assessment continues.**\n- `tests/authoring_cli.rs#fn[explicit_ignored_reads_return_an_error_and_the_assessment_continues]` has the model call `habeas` on a git-ignored file.\n  - The second request contains `untracked.txt` and \"excluded\". It does not contain the file's content.\n  - The evidence output omits the file.\n  - Usage shows two requests, outcome `completed`, and one `habeas` tool failure.\n- `tests/authoring_batch.rs#fn[a_denied_read_returns_an_error_and_its_assessment_continues]` shows the same in batch mode. The denied assessment makes a second request and completes, and the denied file is absent from its evidence.\n- `src/authoring/mod.rs#mod[tests]/fn[a_read_through_a_symlink_leaving_the_project_returns_an_error_to_the_model]` covers a path-based denial. The delivered tool error names `src/escape.rs` and \"outside\", the secret content is absent, and the file is not recorded.\n- `src/authoring/tools.rs` has direct dispatch tests for denials across tools:\n  - `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs` checks that an ignored file's error names `notes.txt` and \"excluded\".\n  - `requests_through_symlinks_leaving_the_project_are_denials` and `unpermitted_requests_outside_the_project_are_recoverable_tool_errors` cover `habeas` by line and by item, `outline`, `ripgrep` and `list_files`. Each error names the path and \"outside\", and no inputs are recorded.\n  - `source_tools_share_sdk_visibility_for_untracked_files` has `outline` and `habeas` fail on the ignored file and succeed on the allowed one.\n\n**2. Discovery and search omit excluded files.**\n- `source_tools_share_sdk_visibility_for_untracked_files` checks `list_files`, `ripgrep` and `ast_grep`.\n  - Ignored files and directories are absent from listings.\n  - Ignored files and directories are absent from matches, including when the search path names an excluded file or directory.\n  - Allow and disallow rules override ignore rules.\n- `search_records_nothing_clamps_at_eof_and_reports_failures` confirms that an ignored hidden directory is omitted while a non-ignored hidden directory is found.\n- `references_list_names_and_flattened_sites_without_recording_inputs` shows that the disallowed `private/notes.md` cite site is omitted from the `references` results.\n\n**3. Malformed arguments and ordinary read failures return explanatory tool errors.**\n- `malformed_and_failed_reads_return_to_the_model_and_the_assessment_continues` covers a wrong-typed `line_start`, a missing form, conflicting forms, a missing file, an absent item and an out-of-range line.\n  - Each failure is not `PermissionDenied`.\n  - Each failure message is delivered in the second request.\n  - The assessment continues and the file is not recorded.\n- Further argument and failure tests:\n  - `failed_listings_return_explanatory_tool_errors`\n  - `search_records_nothing_clamps_at_eof_and_reports_failures`, which covers invalid arguments and syntax errors\n  - `ast_grep_returns_innermost_nodes_of_the_language_and_reports_failures`\n  - `outline_lists_nested_nodes_without_text_or_inputs`\n  - `additional_read_flow_searches_outlines_and_reads_a_rust_file`, which covers `github` argument errors\n  - `paged_inputs_carry_their_definitions_and_deliver_only_their_own_inputs`, which covers `next_page` token errors\n- `operating_system_permission_failures_are_ordinary_read_failures` shows OS permission failures are ordinary errors, not denials. It is skipped when the user is root.\n\nThe mandatory-input abort behaviour belongs to the separate refining requirement `requirements.authoring.read_denial.mandatory`, so it is not assessed here. The tests marked for it are marked correctly and are not needed to cover this subject's text.\n\nNo acknowledged gaps exist or are needed.",
  "references": "963cf9c62a49caeeb3abdcc3e89ee74bc9c0400a3a7d4b901a7cf8dc1478fb7c",
